{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>The Elohim of Abraham, the Elohim of Isaac, and the Elohim of Jacob sent me to you; this is My name forever, and this is My memorial to every generation.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): Scripture says — by this name I wish to be called for all eternity, that they mention Me in every generation and say 'the Elohim of Abraham, the Elohim of Isaac, and the Elohim of Jacob.' The added ו״ו is the way of Scriptural style, as in (Exodus 28:18): ״נופך ספיר ויהלום״, and similarly in the book of Micah the Morashthite (Micah 6:4): ״ואשלח לפניך את משה אהרן ומרים״." "<b>And by way of</b> the Midrash — 'this is My name forever (לעלם), and this is My memorial to every generation': the Holy One, blessed be He, said: it is not as I am written that I am read. I am written with י״ה ו״ה and read with א״ד (Aleph-Dalet). And know that this name, as written, was mentioned in the Temple, but not in the rest of the country — there only by epithet." "<b>And so</b> they said in the Midrash on Psalms: R. Hiyya bar Idi said — why did they pronounce the honored name in the Temple as written, but in the country by its epithet? To instill fear of the honored and awesome name, as it is said (Psalms 87): ״נכבדות מדובר בך עיר האלהים סלה״ — 'the honored name is spoken in you,' that is, in the Temple as written; but in the country by its epithet, as it is said, ״עיר האלהים סלה״. And further, the Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: from the day the Temple was destroyed, it is enough for the world to use two letters, as it is said (Psalms 150:6): ״כל הנשמה תהלל יה״. And the explanation of this is: while the Temple stood, not all souls were equal in praise — in the Temple with the explicit name, and in the country by its epithet; but from the time the Temple was destroyed, and the earth was a breath (נשמה), 'all souls (כל הנשמה) praise Yah' — all souls are equal in praise, for they praise only with half the name." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: 'this is My name forever' — the sefirah of Ḥesed and the sefirah of Pesaḥ, and it is 'the Elohim of Abraham, the Elohim of Isaac' mentioned in the verse; 'and this is My memorial' — the attribute of זכור (remembrance), and it is the attribute of Tiferet, regarding which He mentioned 'and the Eloheim of Jacob'; and therefore He added the letter ו״ו, and it is the force drawn to the tenth [sefirah], which is called דור (generation)." "<b>And the opinion of</b> the Ramban, of blessed memory, is that זכרי is the sefirah of Yesod, and the Yesod according to his opinion is the great Sabbath, and it is 'the Elohim of Jacob'; and He associated זכר (memorial/remembrance) with דור ודור (generation to generation), after the manner of Scripture in mentioning the name, because the tenth [sefirah] is called דור, for from it the generations are drawn, and so Scripture says (Isaiah 41:4): ״קורא הדורות מראש״ — and this is the juxtaposition of זכר with דור, for Knesset Israel is the bride of the Sabbath. And this is what the Sabbath said before the Holy One, blessed be He: 'all have a mate, but I have no mate.' The Yesod said thus because it is the decisive faculty, and the Yesod is the attribute of truth — the seventh of the thirteen attributes, for 'abundant kindness' is said of Tiferet and 'truth' of Yesod. And therefore the language of זכר is said of the Yesod, and the sign is (Proverbs 10:7): ״זכר צדיק לברכה״." "<b>And according to</b> this, the addition of the ו״ו in ואלהי יעקב is to say that it is the deciding element, and every deciding element contains masculinity. And according to the explanation of the verse, ״this is My name forever״ — ״this is My masculine (זכרי) for all generations״ — the term זכרי is the force of mercy, whether it be in Tiferet or in Yesod, for Yesod is the source of blessings; as it is written, ״זכר צדיק לברכה.״ And concerning this it is said (Psalms 145:17): ״צדיק ה׳ בכל דרכיו״ — for the ways of the world and all its operations are entrusted to Him; and because He inclines in His decision toward חסד, it says ״וחסיד בכל מעשיו״; and He is near to all who call upon Him, and the desire of those who fear Him He does. But ״שומר ה׳ את כל אוהביו״ is said of the tenth sefirah adjacent to Him; and this is clear. And furthermore, ״this is My name forever״ alludes that the special Name bears 12 permutations, which are 12 houses, which are 48 letters; and this is what you find in tractate Sukkah: Ahitophel carried a ק״ו by himself — what does it matter to make peace between a man and his wife? The Torah said: My name, which is written in holiness in 48 letters, is erased upon the waters to make peace for the entire world — all the more so how much and how much. And this is clear."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {2 "Read לעלם (without the vav) as the text appears in the comment; this matches certain traditions of the verse's spelling. The phrase והארץ נשמה is taken hyper-literally; possible textual difficulty not smoothed.", 3 "Transliterated divine-name forms exactly as written (אלהי → Elohei/Elohim). The sefirotic allusions are rendered literally without expansion, per Kabbalah-rail.", 4 "Reading מכריע hyper-literally as 'decisive faculty'; the Rambanic sefirotic argument is rendered verbatim without interpretation."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:56:13.514191491Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}